# Batch webhook triggers (no circular hell)

Portal batch emails: `batches` INSERT/UPDATE → edge `batch-updates` → (unpaid/processing) `batch-create`.

## Do

- **Link items first**, then bump unpaid audit fields (`updated_at` / `updated_by`, optionally `validate_at`) so advice sees bills/recharges. Use `touchBatchForAdvice` or `/api/batch/add-items` when **adding to an existing unpaid batch**.
- Prefer `/api/batch/add-items` over client-side `prepaid_recharge`/`bills` updates when adding to an existing batch.
- Let edge functions own `batch_create_url` / `batch_advice_url` / `batch_receipt_url`.
- **Create batch**: rely on INSERT → webhook → `batch-create` retries. Do **not** post-link touch on create (that double-sends advice once unpaid non-URL refresh is allowed).

## Don't

- **Don't** UPDATE `batches` *before* linking items just to “wake” the webhook (empty-advice race).
- **Don't** write `batch_*_url` from the app (edge write-back must skip email via URL-change guard).
- **Don't** bounce `batch_status` (e.g. unpaid→processing→unpaid) to force mail — that is a fake transition and can duplicate Processed/Advice paths.
- **Don't** invoke `batch-create` from the app *and* also poke `batches` for the same add — pick one intentional signal.
- **Don't** remove the edge `statusChanged` / URL-write-back skip without a replacement loop guard.
- **Don't** touch `batches` after create solely for advice — INSERT already triggers it.

## Why unpaid touch works

`batch-updates` re-runs `batch-create` for **unpaid** updates when status is unchanged **and** URL columns did not change (app item-add touch). It **skips** when only URL columns changed (PDF upload write-back) and never re-sends **processing** without a real status transition.
